Repository License And Provenance Boundary

Copyright (c) 2019-2026 Jie Huang, David M. Levinson, Jiaoe Wang,
Haitao Jin, and repository contributors

This repository is a mixed research package. The license below applies only
to materials that the paper authors or repository maintainers have rights to
license, and it does not relicense publication PDFs, controlled smart-card
records, public-agency or data-holder materials, vendor file-format
structures, or third-party materials.

## Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International

Author-created repository documentation, package metadata, source-decision
notes, closeout records, public reference metadata, data dictionaries,
manifests, and rights-cleared derived package metadata are licensed under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0):

https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

This license also covers the staged aggregate AWR formula-check workbook and
CSV in `data/derived_non_sensitive/` only to the extent they consist of
author-created selection, tabulation, formulas, or analysis controlled by the
paper authors or repository maintainers.

## Materials Not Relicensed

This repository license does not apply to:

- The publication PDF under `paper/`, which retains its publisher,
  repository, or manuscript terms.
- Raw Beijing subway smart-card records, card IDs, boarding/alighting traces,
  individual passenger records, station-level trace datasets, SQL Server
  source extracts, raw or de-identified smart-card datasets, and related
  data-holder-controlled source records.
- Beijing Subway, public-agency, institutional, proprietary, confidential, or
  third-party source materials.
- Microsoft Excel, LibreOffice, OpenXML, CSV, or other vendor/runtime/file
  format structures and application metadata.
- Drafts, preprints, reviewer correspondence, submission files, cited
  references, and other third-party or externally controlled materials.

## Software Boundary

No executable software, scripts, notebooks, model source code, SQL extraction
workflow, rule-processing scripts, or paper-specific runtime code are staged
in this repository. This root license therefore grants no separate software
license.
